From: UOS Deepin Podman Maintainers <uos-maintainers@uniontech.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0800
Subject: rootless: preserve systemd socket activation fds across re-exec

When podman.service is socket-activated at user login and races with the
other podman units (podman-restart.service, podman-auto-update.service,
podman-clean-transient.service) to set up the rootless pause process, the
re-executed child can lose the race for the pause PID file.  In that case
podman falls back to reexec_userns_join(), which forks again.

The parent of reexec_in_user_namespace() used to close the LISTEN_FDS
socket (fd 3) before this fallback.  As a result the final child inherited
a stale fd at fd 3 (the user-namespace handle, which is closed by CLOEXEC
at exec), so the journald datagram socket then reused fd 3.  The API
service subsequently tried to accept(2) on a datagram socket and failed
with "accept4: operation not supported", leaving podman.service failed at
boot while a manual restart worked.

Stop closing the activation fds in the parent; they are released when the
parent exits after the child terminates.

---
 pkg/rootless/rootless_linux.c | 19 ++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/pkg/rootless/rootless_linux.c b/pkg/rootless/rootless_linux.c
index ddb97b3..273dbf6 100644
--- a/pkg/rootless/rootless_linux.c
+++ b/pkg/rootless/rootless_linux.c
@@ -981,17 +981,14 @@ reexec_in_user_namespace (int ready, char *pause_pid_file_path)
     {
       if (do_socket_activation)
         {
-          long num_fds;
-
-          num_fds = strtol (saved_systemd_listen_fds, NULL, 10);
-          if (num_fds != LONG_MIN && num_fds != LONG_MAX)
-            {
-              int f;
-
-              for (f = 3; f < num_fds + 3; f++)
-                if (is_fd_inherited (f))
-                  close (f);
-            }
+          /* Do not close the systemd socket activation file descriptors here.
+             If the re-executed child loses the race for the pause PID file, we
+             fall back to reexec_userns_join(), which forks again and needs
+             these fds to remain open so that the final child can inherit the
+             listen socket.  Closing them here would make the final child end
+             up with a reused (e.g. journald) datagram socket at fd 3, breaking
+             the API service with "accept4: operation not supported".  The fds
+             are released when this process exits after the child terminates.  */
           unsetenv ("LISTEN_PID");
           unsetenv ("LISTEN_FDS");
           unsetenv ("LISTEN_FDNAMES");
